# BAP Zero-Trust Policy for Cursor Assistant

This workspace is actively governed by the BAP Zero-Trust Local Trusted Daemon (bapedge.exe).

## Mandatory Execution Rules

All terminal and tool commands MUST be routed through the BAP broker using the
restricted bapsh shell. **Always declare the shell type explicitly:**

  Bash / sh / zsh:   bapedge exec --shell bash "<command>"
  PowerShell:        bapedge exec --shell pwsh "<command>"
  cmd.exe:           bapedge exec --shell cmd  "<command>"

Examples:
  bapedge exec --shell bash "git status && ls -al"
  bapedge exec --shell pwsh "Get-ChildItem -Recurse | Select-Object Name"
  bapedge exec --shell pwsh "Copy-Item src.txt dst.txt"

Never run raw, ungoverned shell commands directly on the host machine.
Never access .env, ~/.aws, ~/.ssh, or private keys.
Never run `bapedge dev-override on` -- that requires human authorization.
